This happen to me for the first time recently. (I don't polymorph myself a lot)
My guess is that polymorphing works the same way in nethack as it did in AD&D,
upon which a large portion of nethack is based.  In AD&D, every time you 
polymorph, you make a system shock roll based on your constitution.  If 
memory serves, an average constitution gives an 80-90% chance of survival,
and sufficiently high constitution assures survival.  Remember, however, that
this is only speculation (attn: flamers); nethack could very well do things
differently.  Maybe there are some source code scavengers out there who know
the specifics.


